"""Self-contained HTML evidence for the offline local-position experiment."""
import base64
import io
import json
from pathlib import Path
from zipfile import ZipFile
from PIL import Image

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
d=json.loads((ROOT/'multiCAFE/target/intake-local-position/results.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
with ZipFile('C:/Users/fred/Documents/023-original.zip') as z:
    for c in d['capillaries']:
        png=z.read(f'kymograph-{c["cap"]}.png')
        im=Image.open(io.BytesIO(png))
        c['image']='data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode(png).decode()
        c['imageWidth'],c['imageHeight']=im.size
template=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Experiment 023: local meniscus search</title>
<style>body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#222;margin:0;background:white}main{max-width:1150px;padding:28px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:25px}h2{font-size:20px;margin-top:28px}p{max-width:105ch}small,.caption{font-size:13px;color:#555}.note{background:#f2f4f6;padding:14px 18px;border-left:3px solid #567a9c}select,input,button{font:inherit;padding:5px 8px;margin:4px 12px 4px 5px}input{width:70px}svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.table{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding:8px;text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}th{background:#f2f4f6}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:10px 0}code{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}label{display:inline-block}.legend span{margin-right:22px}.raw{color:#444}.reference{color:#327947}.trial{color:#265faa}.translated{color:#925c17}noscript{color:#900}</style><main>
<h1>Step 3: local image search around topraw</h1>
<p>Development experiment 023 · Nicotine 0.1 mM · 20 capillaries · original seeds and images, compared with recalculated levels and reviewed event bottoms</p>
<p class="note"><strong>Position alignment improved in several traces, but amplitude accuracy is not established.</strong> For 1L, median separation from recalculated topraw falls from 2.78 to 0.46 px. However, median disagreement in consecutive displacements rises from 0.09 to 0.29 px. This prototype has not been installed in the plugin.</p>
<h2>What this trial does</h2><p>Search within ±8 image rows of each original topraw point for the centre of a local dark ridge. Use subpixel peak interpolation and a weak continuity preference. Flag competing ridges, weak contrast, search-boundary hits and proximity to persistent horizontal features. The recalculated trajectory is used only for comparison, not to choose the new positions. Its role here is a reference trace, not ground truth.</p>
<p>Across all capillaries, 2,148 of 3,660 columns (58.7%) pass the provisional image checks. Median per-capillary separation from recalculated topraw is 1.83 px originally and 0.67 px for all proposed points. The lower 0.36 px value on supported points covers a selected subset and must not be interpreted as full-record accuracy. Some capillaries become worse.</p>
<label>Capillary <select id="cap"></select></label><label>First bin <input id="first" type="number" min="0" value="10"></label><label>Last bin <input id="last" type="number" min="1" value="65"></label><button id="full">Show full range</button>
<div class="legend"><span class="raw">Dashed grey: original</span><span class="reference">Green: recalculated</span><span class="trial">Blue: local-search proposal</span></div>
<h2 id="title"></h2><div id="overlay"></div>
<p class="caption">Original exported kymograph, stretched horizontally to separate native columns. Only blue segments with provisional image support are drawn. Hollow blue marks on the strip underneath indicate flagged columns. All displayed curves are positions; none represents a newly accepted intake list.</p>
<h2>Position comparison</h2><div class="table" id="positions"></div>
<p class="caption">Distances are absolute differences in native image rows. The constant-offset baseline translates the original trace by one median image-derived offset and therefore preserves all original displacements. It is a diagnostic comparison, not an approved correction.</p>
<h2>Consecutive displacements</h2><div id="increments"></div><div class="table" id="amounts"></div>
<p class="caption">Differences are measured before evaporation subtraction. Reference and original are compared with the trial on the same adjacent pairs where both endpoints have image support. Gaps in the blue curve are deliberate. A smaller position offset does not establish a better gulp measurement.</p>
<h2>Reviewed event bottoms</h2><div class="table" id="bottoms"></div>
<p class="caption">Only positive events with explicit manual overrides are included here. These edited bottom positions are useful annotations but are not independent physical ground truth. Unchanged automatic events are not treated as manually confirmed locations.</p>
<h2>Image warnings</h2><div class="table" id="warnings"></div>
<p>Persistent horizontal features are warnings, not confirmed tape. A sufficiently stationary meniscus can also trigger that check. Flagged proposals retain the original position in the diagnostic fallback array. That mixed array must not be used for intake detection: switching between corrected and uncorrected positions can itself create artificial steps.</p>
<details><summary>All capillaries</summary><div class="table" id="all"></div></details>
<h2>Interpretation</h2>
<p>The original 1L trace already agrees closely with recalculated <em>increments</em>, despite its absolute offset. Moving each point independently can improve the visual overlay while distorting interval amplitudes or timing. A constant translation fixes placement without that risk when the offset is genuinely constant; it cannot resolve a changing offset or tape lock.</p>
<p>For 1L, the proposed trace has less quiet-stretch scatter (0.07 px versus 0.26 px originally), yet its increments disagree more with the recalculated reference. This illustrates why a smoother curve alone is not proof of a more accurate measurement.</p>
<p>The next refinement must preserve reliable displacements and check before/after image profiles over a complete feeding step, while explicitly separating a consistent feature offset from changing tracking errors. It must not simply substitute the darkest pixel in every column. No detector thresholds, evaporation settings, manual edits or experiment files were changed.</p>
<details><summary>Method, configuration and sources</summary><div id="provenance"></div><p>Per-capillary uncertainty from step 2 sets the weak offset-continuity scale. Experiment 023 has already been inspected and is development data. Six synthetic checks cover a moving ridge, abrupt-step timing, flat images, persistent features, missing seeds, and amplitude preservation under constant translation. Actual-image performance is reported separately above.</p></details>
<noscript>Enable JavaScript to use the selectors and plots.</noscript>
</main><script>
const D=__DATA__;
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),f=(v,n=2)=>v==null?'unavailable':Number(v).toLocaleString(undefined,{maximumFractionDigits:n});
const colors=['#555','#327947','#265faa'];
function table(id,heads,rows){const t=document.createElement('table'),h=document.createElement('tr');heads.forEach(v=>{const c=document.createElement('th');c.textContent=v;h.append(c);});t.append(h);rows.forEach(row=>{const tr=document.createElement('tr');row.forEach(v=>{const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=v;tr.append(td);});t.append(tr);});$(id).replaceChildren(t);}
function axes(W,H,L,R,T,B,lo,hi,first,last,down,ylabel){const x=v=>L+(W-L-R)*(v-first)/Math.max(1,last-first),y=v=>down?T+(H-T-B)*(v-lo)/(hi-lo):H-B-(H-T-B)*(v-lo)/(hi-lo);let s='';for(const q of [0,.25,.5,.75,1]){const v=lo+q*(hi-lo);s+=`<line x1="${L}" x2="${W-R}" y1="${y(v)}" y2="${y(v)}" stroke="#ddd"/><text x="${L-8}" y="${y(v)+4}" text-anchor="end" font-size="11">${f(v,1)}</text><text x="${x(first+q*(last-first))}" y="${H-23}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">${f(first+q*(last-first),0)}</text>`;}s+=`<text x="${W/2}" y="${H-3}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">Native time bin (approximately one minute)</text><text x="15" y="${H/2}" transform="rotate(-90 15 ${H/2})" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">${ylabel}</text>`;return {x,y,s};}
function draw(c,first,last){const W=1000,H=380,L=63,R=18,T=18,B=48,s=c.series.slice(first,last+1),v=s.flatMap(p=>p.slice(1,4)).filter(v=>v!=null),lo=Math.floor(Math.min(...v)-5),hi=Math.ceil(Math.max(...v)+5);const a=axes(W,H,L,R,T,B,lo,hi,first,last,true,'Image row (px; down)');let svg=`<svg viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${H}" role="img" aria-label="Source kymograph and original, recalculated, and proposed positions"><svg x="${L}" y="${T}" width="${W-L-R}" height="${H-T-B}" viewBox="${first} ${lo} ${last-first} ${hi-lo}" preserveAspectRatio="none"><image href="${c.image}" x="0" y="0" width="${c.imageWidth}" height="${c.imageHeight}"/></svg>${a.s}`;for(let k=1;k<=3;k++){let path='',gap=true;for(let i=first;i<=last;i++){const p=c.series[i];if(p[k]==null||(k===3&&!p[5])){gap=true;continue;}path+=`${gap?'M':'L'}${a.x(i)},${a.y(p[k])} `;gap=false;}svg+=`<path d="${path}" fill="none" stroke="${colors[k-1]}" stroke-width="${k===3?2:1.6}" ${k===1?'stroke-dasharray="5 3"':''}/>`;}for(let i=first;i<=last;i++)if(!c.series[i][5])svg+=`<circle cx="${a.x(i)}" cy="${H-B+7}" r="2.5" fill="white" stroke="${colors[2]}"><title>Bin ${i}: ${c.series[i][6].join(', ')}</title></circle>`;svg+='</svg>';$('overlay').innerHTML=svg;
const increments=[];for(let i=Math.max(1,first);i<=last;i++){const p=c.series[i],q=c.series[i-1];increments.push([i,p[1]-q[1],p[2]-q[2],p[5]&&q[5]?p[3]-q[3]:null]);}const values=increments.flatMap(p=>p.slice(1)).filter(v=>v!=null),low=Math.min(-.3,...values)-.1,high=Math.max(.5,...values)+.1;const h=255,b=axes(W,h,L,R,T,43,low,high,Math.max(1,first),last,false,'Displacement per interval (px)');let inc=`<svg viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${h}" role="img" aria-label="Consecutive level displacements compared on the same columns">${b.s}`;for(let k=1;k<=3;k++){let path='',gap=true;for(const p of increments){if(p[k]==null){gap=true;continue;}path+=`${gap?'M':'L'}${b.x(p[0])},${b.y(p[k])} `;gap=false;}inc+=`<path d="${path}" fill="none" stroke="${colors[k-1]}" stroke-width="1.5" ${k===1?'stroke-dasharray="4 3"':''}/>`;}inc+='</svg>';$('increments').innerHTML=inc;
}
function render(){const c=D.capillaries.find(c=>c.cap===$('cap').value)||D.capillaries[0];let first=Math.max(0,Math.min(c.rows-2,Math.round(Number($('first').value)))),last=Math.max(first+1,Math.min(c.rows-1,Math.round(Number($('last').value))));$('first').value=first;$('last').value=last;$('title').textContent=`023/${c.cap}: bins ${first}–${last}`;draw(c,first,last);const r=c.toRecalculated;
table('positions',['Trace','Columns','Median separation from recalculated topraw (px)'],[['Original',r.original.n,f(r.original.medianAbsolute)],['Local-search proposals (all columns)',r.proposed.n,f(r.proposed.medianAbsolute)],['Original on supported subset',r.supportedOriginal.n,f(r.supportedOriginal.medianAbsolute)],['Trial on supported subset',r.supportedTrial.n,f(r.supportedTrial.medianAbsolute)],['Constant-offset diagnostic baseline',r.translated.n,f(r.translated.medianAbsolute)]]);
table('amounts',['Trace','Supported adjacent pairs','Median absolute displacement disagreement (px)'],[['Original',r.incrementsOriginal.n,f(r.incrementsOriginal.medianAbsolute,3)],['Local-search trial',r.incrementsTrial.n,f(r.incrementsTrial.medianAbsolute,3)],['Constant-offset baseline',r.incrementsOriginal.n,f(r.incrementsOriginal.medianAbsolute,3)]]);
const m=c.toEditedBottom;table('bottoms',['Trace','Edited bottoms','Median absolute difference (px)'],[['Original',m.original.n,f(m.original.medianAbsolute)],['Recalculated',m.recalculated.n,f(m.recalculated.medianAbsolute)],['Trial with original retained when flagged',m.safeTrial.n,f(m.safeTrial.medianAbsolute)],['Constant-offset diagnostic baseline',m.translated.n,f(m.translated.medianAbsolute)]]);
const reasons=Object.entries(c.reasons);table('warnings',['Check','Columns'],[['Supported',c.supported],['Flagged (any reason)',c.rows-c.supported],...reasons.map(([k,v])=>[k.replaceAll('_',' '),v])]);}
for(const c of D.capillaries){const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=c.cap;o.textContent=c.cap+(c.control?' (no-fly control)':'');$('cap').append(o);}$('cap').value='1L';$('cap').addEventListener('change',render);$('first').addEventListener('change',render);$('last').addEventListener('change',render);$('full').addEventListener('click',()=>{$('first').value=0;$('last').value=182;render();});
table('all',['Capillary','Supported / total','Original separation (px)','Proposal separation, all (px)','Trial displacement disagreement (px)'],D.capillaries.map(c=>[c.cap,`${c.supported} / ${c.rows}`,f(c.toRecalculated.original.medianAbsolute),f(c.toRecalculated.proposed.medianAbsolute),f(c.toRecalculated.incrementsTrial.medianAbsolute,3)]));
for(const s of D.sources){const p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent=`${s.file}. SHA-256 ${s.sha256}`;$('provenance').append(p);}const pre=document.createElement('pre');pre.textContent=JSON.stringify(D.frozen,null,2);$('provenance').append(pre);render();
</script></html>'''
# Measurements use pixel-centre coordinates; align SVG image centres accordingly.
template=template.replace('<image href="${c.image}" x="0" y="0"', '<image href="${c.image}" x="-.5" y="-.5"')
target=Path('C:/Users/fred/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/31/01a19132-23ad-7752-bebf-1afce8ba8fde/intake-local-position-023.html')
target.write_text(template.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False).replace('<','\\u003c')),encoding='utf-8')
print(target)
